# Local SUPERHOT game install, used only for local build/testing (SuperhotGameDir points
# here) -- this is a full copy of the actual commercial game (SH.exe, SH_Data/ assets,
# etc.), never something to commit or publish. Critical: must stay ignored even though it
# sits at the project root alongside apworld/ and mod/.
/SUPERHOT/

# .NET build output (mod/SuperhotArchipelago/)
bin/
obj/
*.user

# Python bytecode cache (apworld/superhot/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor/OS cruft
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Internal working notes -- kept locally for our own reference, deliberately not part of
# the public repo. TESTING.md's user-facing content now lives inline in README.md instead.
/TESTING.md
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/NOTES.md
/MOD_GUIDE.md

# Release-notes staging doc -- kept locally only (explicit user request), not pushed to
# GitHub. Unlike the other gitignored docs above, this one is meant to become public
# content eventually (copied into GitHub Release notes), it just isn't tracked as a repo
# file itself.
/CHANGELOG.md

# Packaged mod release zips (Nexus and Thunderstore alike) -- these are built
# distribution artifacts (Mods/ + UserLibs/, built from mod/SuperhotArchipelago's own
# build output), not source, and don't belong in git history. They get attached to
# GitHub Releases directly instead of committed. The apworld's built copy is still
# tracked at dist/superhot.apworld since that one *is* meant to live in a GitHub
# release built from this repo.
#
# Real bug found while auditing repo hygiene: the original pattern here
# (SuperhotArchipelago_v*.zip) didn't match the Thunderstore zip's actual filename
# (SuperhotArchipelago_thunderstore_v*.zip), so it kept slipping through and getting
# tracked anyway. Broadened to catch any packaged zip under dist/, not just the Nexus
# naming scheme.
dist/*.zip
